1
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Cetus-Lupedus! She's back!

2
00:08:54,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Zenon: The Zequel is a family, tv movie, adventure film directed by Manny Coto.

3
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Zenon Kar is 15 and lives on a space station which the
military has taken over and is dismantling.

4
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:54,000
She receives a mysterious signal and must convince everyone
that it's from aliens who have come to help them.

5
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:21,000
Zenon Kar, played by Kirsten Storms.

6
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Nebula Wade, played by Shadia Simmons.

7
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Margie Hammond, played by Lauren Maltby.

8
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Astrid Kar, played by Susan Brady.

9
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:09,000
Mark Kar, played by Robert Curtis Brown.

10
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:36,000
Proto Zoa, played by Phillip Rhys.

11
00:48:57,000 --> 00:49:03,000
Zenon: The Zequel is a 2001 American science fiction
comedy film directed by Manny Coto.

12
00:53:24,000 --> 00:53:30,000
It is the second installment of the Disney Channel's Zenon television film series, following the first
installment, Zenon: Girl of the 21st Century (1999), and preceding Zenon: Z3 (2004).

13
00:57:51,000 --> 00:57:57,000
The film premiered on Disney Channel on January 12, 2001.

14
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:24,000
The film is also the first sequel to be produced under
the Disney Channel Original Movie banner.

15
01:06:45,000 --> 01:06:51,000
This is the only Zenon film where Raven-Symoné does not play Nebula.

16
01:11:12,000 --> 01:11:18,000
She is replaced by Shadia Simmons.

17
01:15:39,000 --> 01:15:45,000
The Disney Channel Original Series Lizzie McGuire
premiered after the film's premiere.

18
01:20:06,000 --> 01:20:12,000
This is the last film directed by Manny Coto before his death in 2023.

19
01:24:33,000 --> 01:24:39,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
